   "source": [
    "# Project 4: Data Type Memory & Performance Benchmark Lab"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2c73f5e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Objective:** see how the dtype (int8 to int64, float16 to float64) changes memory, speed and precision."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b7264f08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import timeit\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5e238ef6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Make the same array in every dtype"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "289c3fed",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1 million numbers from 0 to 99 (0-99 fits in int8)\n",
    "base = np.arange(1000000) % 100\n",
    "\n",
    "names = [\"int8\", \"int16\", \"int32\", \"int64\", \"float16\", \"float32\", \"float64\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "arrays = {}\n",
    "for n in names:\n",
    "    arrays[n] = base.astype(n)\n",
    "\n",
    "for n in names:\n",
    "    print(n, arrays[n][:5])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9f6a1226",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: size, itemsize and nbytes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "501ca4e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"dtype    size    itemsize    nbytes\")\n",
    "mem = []\n",
    "for n in names:\n",
    "    a = arrays[n]\n",
    "    print(n, a.size, a.itemsize, a.nbytes)\n",
    "    mem.append(a.nbytes / 1024 / 1024)   # in MB"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5fe3bd14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "itemsize is bytes per number. int8 = 1 byte, int64 = 8 bytes, so int8 uses 8x less memory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a24a2481",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Time sum and multiply"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5f6110e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sum_time = []\n",
    "mul_time = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for n in names:\n",
    "    arr = arrays[n]\n",
    "    t1 = timeit.timeit(\"arr.sum()\", globals=globals(), number=100) / 100 * 1000\n",
    "    t2 = timeit.timeit(\"arr * 2\", globals=globals(), number=100) / 100 * 1000\n",
    "    sum_time.append(t1)\n",
    "    mul_time.append(t2)\n",
    "    print(n, \"sum:\", round(t1, 3), \"ms   multiply:\", round(t2, 3), \"ms\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1e771d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Smaller types are faster for multiply. float16 is slow because the CPU has no fast support for it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f8eeb05d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for n in names:\n",
    "    print(n, arrays[n].sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe04ec8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "float16 sum gives inf because its max value is 65504 and the real sum is about 49 million."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1e34e40",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Overflow and precision loss"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "397c1f14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(np.iinfo(np.int8))\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.array([100, 127, 128, 200, 300])\n",
    "print(x.astype(np.int8))\n",
    "print(x.astype(np.int16))\n",
    "\n",
    "a = np.array([100], dtype=np.int8)\n",
    "print(a + a)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "db638c37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "int8 can only hold -128 to 127, so 200 wraps around to -56. There is no error, so it is easy to miss."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d330b8d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(np.finfo(np.float16))\n",
    "print(np.finfo(np.float32))\n",
    "print(np.finfo(np.float64))\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.float64(1234.56789123456789)\n",
    "print(x)\n",
    "print(x.astype(np.float32))\n",
    "print(x.astype(np.float16))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(np.float16(0.1) + np.float16(0.2))\n",
    "print(np.float64(0.1) + np.float64(0.2))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(np.float64(70000).astype(np.float16))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d1dbf2e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "float16 keeps about 3 digits, float32 about 7 and float64 about 15. float16 cannot store anything above 65504 (gives inf)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c984d594",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Memory vs time charts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8a391a89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(15, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 3, 1)\n",
    "plt.bar(names, mem)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Memory (MB)\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 3, 2)\n",
    "plt.bar(names, sum_time, color=\"orange\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Sum time (ms)\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.subplot(1, 3, 3)\n",
    "plt.bar(names, mul_time, color=\"green\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Multiply time (ms)\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
